1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """EVERY STAGE RUNS THE FULL PANEL BEFORE THE ROUND MOVES ON.
3: 
4: Owner directive, 2026-08-16, and it SUPERSEDES the carrier's older rule of "ONE full
5: panel per ROUND, with pass 2 restricted to codex + Opus".  That older rule was written
6: when Grok's free tier was dead and Kimi was quota-dead; both are healthy now, all seven
7: scriptable seats answered the last three panels, and the only live constraint is that the
8: three Ollama seats return HTTP 429 if two panels fire within ~20 minutes -- a spacing that
9: real stages already exceed.
10: 
11: THE RULE: for any stage (assess / research / review) that ran ON OR AFTER the cutoff, all
12: nine seats must be recorded.  If a seat cannot be run, the round STOPS and the owner is
13: asked -- degrading silently is exactly what this replaces.
14: 
15: TWO DELIBERATE EXEMPTIONS, both owner directives, both narrow:
16: 
17:   * `regress` is FABLE-ONLY.  Only the flagship seat reviews regression, batched.
18:   * stages that ran BEFORE the cutoff are GRANDFATHERED, forward-only by owner decision.
19:     They are not re-panelled; they carry an explicit annotation entry so the dashboard does
20:     not read their blanks as seat failures.  A blank cell and a seat failure must never look
21:     alike -- that conflation is what this whole layer exists to prevent.
22: 
23: Exit 0 clean, 1 on violations.  `--list` shows every stage checked.
24: """
25: import json
26: import os
27: import sys
28: 
29: sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
30: import stage_tokens as st   # #534: the ONE place a token is spelled or classified
31: 
32: HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
33: #  Overridable so controls run against COPIES.  Added 2026-08-17 after a negative control
34: #  for the CLOSED-WHILE-HELD clause silently tested NOTHING: it wrote a mutated ledger to a
35: #  temp file, passed $GXLEDGER, and this script -- which had no such override -- read the real
36: #  ledger and reported PASS.  A VOID CONTROL AND A PASSING CONTROL ARE INDISTINGUISHABLE in
37: #  the output, which is the failure mode the whole harness is built against.
38: LEDGER = os.environ.get("GXLEDGER") or os.path.join(HERE, "ledger.json")
39: 
40: CUTOFF = "2026-08-16"          # stages dated on or after this must be complete
41: 
42: #  ---- HOLD QUESTIONS -----------------------------------------------------------------
43: #  A STAGE HELD *FOR* A SEAT MUST CARRY THE QUESTION IT IS HELD FOR.  That rule has been in
44: #  CLAUDE.md since a 46-row batch measured it: the three meta-rows carrying identical
45: #  boilerplate had their question RECONSTRUCTED from the row's subject, while the two that
46: #  named it explicitly were the easiest to answer *accurately*.
47: #
48: #  *** IT WAS AT 0 FOR 18 ON 2026-08-26. ***  Every held stage in the ledger carried a
49: #  DISPOSITION note where a question belongs -- "FILE - no measurable effect until a caller
50: #  survives", "a policy, not a round".  Each is a true statement about the row.  None is a
51: #  question a seat can answer.
52: #
53: #  This is the carrier diagnosing itself: the rule was PROSE in an auto-loaded file, it was
54: #  known, and it still did not fire.  A seat given a disposition note must GUESS what it is
55: #  being asked, and a guessed question yields an answer to the wrong question that still
56: #  LOOKS like a discharged stage -- the seat-failure-counted-as-agreement shape, moved one
57: #  step earlier.
58: #
59: #  DATED CUTOFF, owner decision 2026-08-26, and the same shape check_bugfile_sync.py uses:
60: #  stages whose newest entry is on or before HOLDQ_CUTOFF are REPORTED and not failed.  A
61: #  rule that retro-fails 18 pre-existing rows blocks the next commit on reconstruction work
62: #  nobody scheduled, and a rule that does that gets switched off.  New holds are enforced.
63: HOLDQ_CUTOFF = "2026-08-26"
64: FABLE_ONLY = {"regress"}       # owner directive: only the flagship reviews regression
65: STAGES = ("assess", "research", "review")
66: 
67: #  An annotation entry is not a review.  It exists to say WHY a stage is short, and it must
68: #  not be counted as one of the seats that answered -- otherwise marking a gap would close it.
69: ANNOTATION = st.ANNOTATION      # #534: spelled once, in stage_tokens.py
70: 
71: #  A SECOND, DIFFERENT EXEMPTION, and it is deliberately not folded into the first.
72: #
73: #  The token above asserts a specific historical fact: the stage ran before the full-panel
74: #  directive.  On 2026-08-21 a batched flagship pass added a single entry to a row that had been
75: #  FILED with one seat -- and one filing plus one re-read is counted here as a TWO-OF-NINE STAGE,
76: #  so section H reddened for a row nobody had convened a panel on.
77: #
78: #  *** THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT CLEARING THAT USED THE TOKEN ABOVE, WHICH WOULD HAVE PUT A FALSE
79: #  STATEMENT IN THE LEDGER TO TURN A GATE GREEN. ***  A 2026-08-21 re-read did not run under the
80: #  pre-2026-08-16 policy.  Backed out; the honest fix is a token that says what actually
81: #  happened, because the two situations are not the same and a reader must be able to tell them
82: #  apart.
83: #
84: #  This is a real recurring category rather than a one-off: any pass that sweeps filed rows can
85: #  promote a filing into a short stage without anyone deciding to.
86: RE_READ = st.RE_READ      # #534: spelled once, in stage_tokens.py
87: 
88: #  A THIRD EXEMPTION, 2026-09-18, and like the second it exists because neither older token was
89: #  TRUE of the situation -- which is the only reason this file ever gains a token.
90: #
91: #  A session read 23 UNREAD SEAT ANSWERS off disk and recorded each onto the row it discussed.
92: #  That is strictly an improvement to the record: this project has three times found real
93: #  defects sitting in an unread review.  **It took both stage gates from GREEN to RED, creating
94: #  19 violations where HEAD had zero** -- because recording a seat's remark about row X makes
95: #  row X's stage go from ABSENT (or a 1-seat filing) to a 2..8-seat "short panel", and a short
96: #  panel is what this check reddens on.
97: #
98: #  *** SO THE GATE FIRED BECAUSE THE RECORD GOT MORE HONEST, AND THE ONLY WAY TO GREEN IT WITH
99: #  THE OLDER TOKENS WOULD HAVE BEEN TO WRITE A FALSE SENTENCE INTO THE LEDGER. ***  RE_READ says
100: #  SINGLE-SEAT, and several of these carry 2, 3, 4, 6 and even 8 recorded seats; ANNOTATION
101: #  asserts a pre-2026-08-16 vintage that is simply untrue of a 2026-09-17 entry.  The comment on
102: #  RE_READ already records the last time someone reached for the nearest token to turn a gate
103: #  green, and that attempt was backed out.  This is that lesson obeyed rather than re-learned.
104: #
105: #  THE DISCRIMINATOR, and it is mechanical rather than a judgement call: read the `ev` field for
106: #  the panel dir, open that dir's `brief_sent.md`, and ask **WAS THIS PANEL CONVENED ON THIS
107: #  ROW?**  If the brief's subject is this row (or a deliberate multi-row late review naming it),
108: #  the stage RAN and this token is a lie.  If the brief is about some other row and a seat merely
109: #  mentioned this one in passing, no panel was ever convened here.
110: #
111: #  *** THAT TEST OVERTURNED THE AUTHOR'S FIRST SORTING, WHICH IS WHY IT IS WRITTEN DOWN AS A
112: #  COMMAND AND NOT AS ADVICE. ***  Seat COUNT was used first -- "+8 seats must mean a real panel"
113: #  -- and it was wrong three times over: `diskimagesign`, `pcc2c040assertrow` and
114: #  `pcc2genctlc040alias` all cite ONE dir, `panel_20260917_100431`, whose brief IS convened on
115: #  them, so they are real stages; while `asiceventaddr` carries a full EIGHT recorded seats that
116: #  all cite `panel_20260826_222557`, a pass 2 on a COMMENT-ONLY commit to a vendored header --
117: #  a different subject entirely, and therefore not a stage at all.  **The count is a CORRELATE
118: #  of "a panel ran"; the brief's subject is the thing itself.
119: #
120: #  *** THE TOKEN STATES THE GENERAL CLAIM AND THE NOTE CARRIES THE SPECIFIC REASON, WHICH IS A
121: #  DELIBERATE BREAK FROM THE TWO TOKENS ABOVE. ***  Those bake their reason into the literal,
122: #  and that is exactly what made RE_READ unusable here -- it says SINGLE-SEAT, so a true
123: #  situation with three seats had no token that fitted.  A first draft of THIS token repeated
124: #  the mistake: it read INCIDENTAL SEAT MENTION, which is true of eleven of the twelve stages
125: #  and FALSE of `ip30abortkill' assess, whose two entries are a rung-3 WITNESS BUILD and a
126: #  ship-order ADJUDICATION -- real work on that very row, and not a panel seat answer at all.
127: #  The checkable claim both gates need is only ever "no panel was convened on this stage";
128: #  everything else is provenance, and provenance belongs in prose a reader can check.**
129: NOPANEL = st.NOPANEL      # #534: spelled once, in stage_tokens.py
130: 
131: #  *** A STAGE DELIBERATELY HELD FOR A NAMED SEAT IS NOT A STAGE THAT MOVED ON. ***
132: #
133: #  Added 2026-08-17.  Fable usage ran high and the owner said to queue Fable work and carry on
134: #  with the rest.  That is the honest thing to do -- eight seats can answer now and the ninth
135: #  when quota returns -- but the first version of this check reported the resulting 8/9 as
136: #  "moved on without the full panel", which is exactly wrong: nothing moved on, the round is
137: #  explicitly open and waiting.  Two different states rendering the same is the defect this
138: #  whole layer exists to prevent, so it must not be committed BY this layer.
139: #
140: #  A HELD marker is an explicit ledger entry carrying this token and NAMING the awaited seats.
141: #  It is reported separately, not as a violation.
142: #
143: #  THE ANTI-LOOPHOLE, and it is the whole reason this is safe to add: a held stage on a CLOSED
144: #  row is a HARD violation.  You may wait for a seat; you may not close a round while waiting
145: #  for one.  Without that clause "HELD" would be a way to mark any gap and walk away, which is
