29663:   "state_note": "[2026-10-18, #566] regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py is wired into gate 14 (regress/gate_arm.sh, 41 checks) and its 2026-10-30 exemption deleted.  Next due: alpha_tbi_probe.py 2026-10-22 and lca_badval 10-23, lca_widewrite 10-26, lca_isalane 10-27 (the other session's), then the four wdc_* probes 11-05 .. 12-03.  The `ip30_abort_probe' entry in the due list below is history.  ||  *** STATUS 2026-10-18 (#565): ppc_rldicl_probe.py WIRED into gate_ppc.sh (gate 13) and its exemption DELETED, five days before it would have refused every commit (dated 2026-10-22; `d < today').  Gate 13 PASS 140 checks, the rldicl block's 30 among them (regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/gatewire_20261018/gate13/).  NEXT DUE: alpha_tbi_probe.py 2026-10-22 -- refuses from 10-23; the other session's Alpha area, so its gate block or an owner re-date is owed; then lca_badval 10-23, lca_widewrite 10-26, lca_isalane 10-27, ip30_abort_probe 10-30 and the four wdc_* probes 11-05..12-03.  THIS ROW STAYS OPEN. ***  ||  *** STATUS 2026-09-18 (GXEMUL): #536 SHIPS -- mk48_nvram_probe.py (57 rows) and hpcmips_ctor_probe.py (28 construction IDs) wired into gate_arm.sh; the other eleven 2026-09-20 exemptions re-dated to 2026-09-27 BY OWNER RULING; the selftest's M5a/M5b days DERIVED from the table, M5a ON the stamped date (the old literals: 21/22; a d <= today mutant: 21/22).  Pass 2 + §F2, nine seats, fable5 LAST: SHIP.  THIS ROW STAYS OPEN: the eleven fall due again as ONE block on 2026-09-28 -- `exemptcliff` owns that; FILED from the round: hpcmipsc2, exemptcal, m5dayb. ***\n\n\n\n**RESIDUAL-REMAINS.**  `8404520` added PIT's completion sentinel, and PIT plus SH4 BSC were\nsubsequently wired.  **Six exemptions remain, all dated 2026-09-20, and the checker rejects them\nfrom the 21st**: `fbpending_drain_probe.py`, `hpcmips_ctor_probe.py`, the three `wdc_altoffset*`\nprobes, and `wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py` -- *which is the carrier for [[wdcaddtoinbufbound]]'s proposed\nclosure, so the two rows are coupled.*\n\n*** THE ROW IS FRAMED AS \"WIRE SIX PROBES\" AND THAT IS THE WRONG JOB.  FOUR OF THE SIX CANNOT SERVE\nAS GATE ROWS AT ALL, AND WIRING THEM ON THE DEADLINE WOULD SHIP FOUR GATE SECTIONS THAT CANNOT FAIL.\nFound by a codex ANALYSIS job 2026-09-08, VERIFIED here. ***\n\nThe cliff is real and was reproduced first: `check_probe_wiring.py --today 2026-09-21` gives\n`PROBEWIRING_FAIL  6 problem(s)`, and `--today 2026-09-19` passes.  The comparison is `d < today`,\nso the exemptions are good THROUGH the 20th and rejected from the 21st.\n\n**codex's finding, which the brief did not ask for:** *\"the signature and 4-bit probes print\nmeasurements without enforcing a pass/fail result ... All four WDC harnesses can finish with exit\nstatus zero after reporting failures.\"*\n\n**MEASURED here, per probe -- count of nonzero-exit paths and of PASS/FAIL tokens:**\n\n    fbpending_drain_probe.py       nonzero-exit 2   tokens PASS/FAIL      ENFORCEABLE\n    hpcmips_ctor_probe.py          nonzero-exit 3   tokens PASS/FAIL/_RESULT=   ENFORCEABLE\n    wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py        nonzero-exit 0   token  FAIL only      *** CANNOT FAIL ***\n    wdc_altoffset_probe.py         nonzero-exit 0   token  FAIL only      *** CANNOT FAIL ***\n    wdc_altoffset_4bit_probe.py    nonzero-exit 1   NO pass/fail token    partial\n    wdc_altoffset_sig_probe.py     nonzero-exit 0   NO pass/fail token    *** CANNOT FAIL ***\n\n> **THREE OF THE SIX HAVE NO NONZERO-EXIT PATH WHATEVER, AND TWO OF THOSE EMIT NO RESULT TOKEN\n> EITHER.  A gate section calling them greps for nothing and tests an exit status that is always 0 --\n> the CHECK-THAT-CANNOT-FAIL class, in its purest form.**\n\n*** AND THE DEADLINE IS WHAT MAKES THIS DANGEROUS RATHER THAN MERELY UNTIDY. ***  On 2026-09-20 the\nchecker starts blocking commits, and the obvious way to unblock it is to add six gate invocations.\n**Four of those would be inert, and the checker would then go GREEN -- it verifies that a gate CALLS\nthe probe, not that the call can fail.**  The cliff would have converted a loud, honest red into a\nquiet, permanent false green, and nothing downstream would ever say so.\n\n*** THE DISPOSITION QUESTION IS THE MANIFEST CLASS, NOT THE WIRING, AND THE CHECKER ITSELF ALREADY\nSAYS SO. ***  Its own output carries:\n\n    note  SELFLABEL  wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py: manifest says detector, its own summary line says\n                     witness.  Advisory only -- self-labels are measurably unreliable in both\n                     directions.\n\n**A WITNESS reproduces a defect on a pre-fix build and is done; a DETECTOR must run forever and must\nbe able to go red.**  Four of these six behave like witnesses or measurement harnesses, and the\nmanifest classes all six as detectors.  So the candidate dispositions are:\n\n  1. **wire the two that enforce** (`fbpending_drain`, `hpcmips_ctor`) -- cheap, and codex names\n     plausible homes: `gate_arm.sh` already supplies the CATS stub for the first,\n     `gate_asan_sweep.sh` covers machine construction for the second;\n  2. for the four, EITHER give each a real verdict line and a nonzero exit -- which makes them\n     detectors in fact rather than by declaration -- OR reclassify them in the manifest, which is a\n     records change with no gate cost;\n  3. NOT: extend the dates.  That is the option the cliff exists to prevent.\n\n**Two corrections to the brief's own premises, both from codex and both checked:** `gate_wdc.sh`\nDOES NOT EXIST (I assumed it might), and `run.sh` runs **16** gates, none of which invokes any of the\nsix -- `gate_hygiene`'s references to them are source-TEXT inspections, not invocations.\n\n*** WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED, said plainly: codex could not run the checker (outside its allowlist),\nso it confirmed the six expiring ENTRIES without independently reproducing \"exactly six problems\".\nI did run it, and got six.  Its timings are source-based estimates and are NOT measured runs -- so\nthe cost side of \"four are cheap\" remains an estimate, and the row should not repeat it as measured.***  *** MEASURED 2026-09-17 BY THE OPUS 5 SEAT, ON A BATCH THAT WAS NOT ASKED ABOUT WIRING -- AND IT IS THE SHARPEST ANSWER IN THAT BATCH TO \"what is the smallest edit that breaks the fix and still passes?\" ***  For four of the nine rows reviewed, **the answer is THE ENTIRE FIX, REVERTED, and the row that stays GREEN is every row in the full battery.**     lca_confbus_probe.py      NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (lcashiftub)\n    lca_confwidth_probe.py    NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (lcaconfwidth, MED)\n    alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py  NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (alphapfnoffset, **HIGH**)\n    alpha_harness_probe.py    NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (alphaswpctxptbr, **HIGH**)\n  -- against the wired controls in the same batch: sh_iprbcd_probe.py, sgi_re_rgb_probe.py, gdrom_default_probe.py and diff_wdc_identify.c all ARE referenced.  `run.sh` runs an explicit `GATES=(...)` list and the four appear nowhere outside `regress/` and the wiring checker itself. *** TWO OF THE FOUR ARE HIGH-SEVERITY ROWS.  Delete `| (vaddr & ((1ULL << pageSizeShift) - 1))` from `memory_alpha.c` and a HIGH page-walk defect is back with a CLEAN BATTERY. *** **THE SEAT EXPLICITLY DECLINED TO CLAIM THIS AS NEW, which is the right call and is why it lands here rather than as a fresh row:** `check_probe_wiring.py` already classifies all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` -- correctly, by the ladder's witness/detector timing line -- and its own entry for `lca_confbus_probe.py` says *\"but this probe RUNS IN NO GATE, so the coverage exists and is never executed: wiringcliff\"*. *** BUT THAT CHECKER IS UNCOMMITTED, so **nothing in any committed tree reports this today.** ***  The four closures are HONEST -- their `witness:` says `probe:`, which is exactly what it is -- and what is absent is STANDING DEFENCE.  The seat's disposition, adopted: this belongs in each round record as a DISCLOSED RESIDUAL on those four rows, not only as one filed id, because a reader of `alphapfnoffset` alone cannot see it.  *** SCOPE NOTE FROM THE FABLE ADJUDICATION, 2026-09-17: MAKE SURE THE FOUR `CLASS_WITNESS` PROBES ARE IN THIS ROW'S SCOPE, NOT ONLY THE DATED EXEMPTIONS. ***  This row's own title is about the EXEMPT table expiring, and the four unwired witnesses (`lca_confbus_probe.py`, `lca_confwidth_probe.py`, `alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py`, `alpha_harness_probe.py`) are a different population -- classified `CLASS_WITNESS`, never exempted, simply never run. *** AND A TRAP THAT WOULD BITE THE FIX: `lca_confwidth_probe.py` MUST NOT BE WIRED AS-IS. ***  It scores **2/6 at HEAD** (measured 2026-09-17, `regress/artifacts/lcaconfwidth/head_20260917/`) because `#518` replaced the IOC_CONF kill with a decline.  Wiring it produces a PHANTOM RED; the remedy there is RE-PIN OR RETIRE, under the oracle-correction rule's order -- re-pin first, measure the committed build red under the new expectations, then change anything. **AND THE COMMITTED TREE ALREADY KNOWS**, which sharpens the gap rather than excusing it: `check_probe_wiring.py` carries all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` with their scores.  *The gap is the FAILING, not the knowing* -- the checker deliberately does not fail on that class.  *** OWNER DECISION 2026-09-17: STAGGER -- wire the cheap ones, re-date the rest with SEPARATED deadlines and the owing round named on each.  A blanket extension was declined for the reason this checker's own header gives: debt that expires, not debt that disappears -- and the present cliff exists because ONE deliberate alignment of two #442 debts was then copied by nine later exemptions. ***  THE ELEVEN ARE NOT ONE JOB.  Derived 2026-09-17 by reading each probe rather than its exemption text, and they fall into FIVE classes: (1) THREE ALPHA PROBES -- alpha_tbi, lca_badval, lca_isalane -- share ONE blocker; (2) FOUR wdc_* probes are TWO-LEG DIFFERENTIALS needing a single-leg mode, and two of those additionally need rig images the battery does not build; (3) fbpending_drain is REPORT-ONLY until EXPECT_CAP is designed; (4) mk48_nvram needs an mvme187 leg on gate_m88k_rounding.sh; (5) ppc_rldicl lacks the RESULT/CONTROL protocol AND is on the do-not-commit list, so it CANNOT be wired at all and must be re-dated whatever else happens.  *** THE FINDING THAT CHANGES THE PLAN, AND IT IS A WRONG PREMISE IN THE EXEMPTION'S OWN REASON.  Measured, not reasoned. ***  All three Alpha entries read 'no gate runs an Alpha machine; gate_crossfamily.sh is the named home and giving it one is a harness round'.  That premise is TRUE OF RIGS AND FALSE OF PROBES.  gate_crossfamily.sh (gate 5) drives BOOTABLE RIG IMAGES through drive_guest.py, so 'an Alpha leg' reads as 'obtain a bootable Alpha guest', which genuinely is a harness round.  But measured against the probes themselves: NONE of the three references a disk image at all; each execs `-E alpha' as a rung-3 COLD-DEBUGGER probe; and each already emits the parseable token a gate scores (ALPHATBI_RESULT, LCABADVAL_RESULT, LCAISALANE_RESULT).  gate_arm.sh already wires probes in exactly this shape -- `python3 <probe>.py \"$BIN\" > \"$LOG\" 2>&1 || true' followed by count rows -- and runs SIX of them.  So what these three need is a PROBE SECTION, not an Alpha rig: roughly six lines apiece in an idiom the tree already uses six times.  ONE gate run discharges all three.  THE STAGGER, therefore: WIRE the three Alpha probes into gate 5 as a probe section (they also fit its stated purpose -- 'non-MIPS CPU cores actually execute guest code' -- since a cold-debugger probe executing real Alpha instructions is precisely that).  RE-DATE the other eight to separated deadlines by CLASS, so the next cliff cannot re-form: the four wdc_* together behind the single-leg-mode instrument change, fbpending_drain behind EXPECT_CAP, mk48_nvram behind the mvme187 leg, ppc_rldicl on its own and longest, since it is blocked by a do-not-commit constraint rather than by work.  NOT DONE IN THIS TURN, DELIBERATELY: the exemption block states that each wiring owes ONE CLEAN GATE RUN proving it green before it ships, citing FOUR probes that shipped latently RED because the commit adding them never fired the gate.  A gate run contends with the #531 measurement in flight, so the wiring lands with its gate run and not before.  The deletion rule is already recorded here and is followed: a wired probe that KEEPS its exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it, so each entry is DELETED in the SAME edit that adds its wiring.",
