30009:     "note": "#566 PASS 1 (the design brief): 4 flags -- GPT-6 Astra: the probe header's CONTRACT is the 27-row instrument's (six announce sites, fourteen latch cells, `THE CLOSURE IS OWED') while the file's own later sections record the finished 33-row closure (TAKEN: a dated note above the CONTRACT, AST unchanged); the load disclosure must name the false green -- a session the 12 s poll kills reports `alive' (TAKEN, narrowed by reading the probe); the `ip30_tick_probe.py' comment's `dated-exempt in the open' (TAKEN); OUTSTANDING_BUGS' `ip30abortkill' entry still says 28 rows, pre-fix owed, pass 2 owed (TAKEN).  Also asked for a good log under a non-zero status, doubled/malformed CONTROL and DONE, a missing probe file and section R's UNWIRED leg (all run: selftest n11-n15, controls/R_CONTROLS.out), and would close `ip30abortkill' in this commit (NOT TAKEN: D1)."
