sigreturn frame, and Linux's `valid_user_regs` rejects anything whose MODE_MASK is not USR/USR26 and forces USR32.  **So the path exists and no correct kernel drives it.** **CONSEQUENCE FOR `armmsrmodekill`:** it stays a real process death and a real fix -- a hostile or buggy guest reaches it, and 25 of 32 encodings are unhandled -- but its SEVERITY is now measured rather than assumed, and it does NOT outrank ip30.  **`highrankunmeasured` is answered on the armmsr side by READING; the ip30 side stands as measured (gate_asan_sweep runs ip30 green, so the aborts are on no in-tree path).**",
50626:   "state_note": "*** CENSUSED 2026-09-17 AND THE CLASS IS CLOSED WITH ITS DENOMINATOR: **0 shipped live probes still mis-score this way.**  The defect was born today and died today. ***  The founding case is `regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py`, which had the exact shape, was MEASURED reporting `alive` for a process that had SIGABRT'd, and was rewritten to poll the same hour.  `arm_msrmode_probe.py` was built with the polling form from the start. **METHOD, keyed on MECHANISM rather than on names** -- and it explicitly refused to count `artifacts/**` frozen copies, which would have inflated the class about FIFTEENFOLD by re-counting the same five files: live population is `regress/*.py` = **99 files**, minus 10 harness/selftest/census scripts and one source-only probe = **88 launchers**. **THE DEATH-AS-ORACLE FAMILIES, with counts:** EOF-as-alive (`alive = rd(...)`) **33**; sessions borrowed from those 33 **11** (pcc2_default execs pcc2_width's session; ten SH4 probes import sh4_pcic_probe); prompt/dump still-answering **3**; `subprocess.run` wait-status **6**; **`WNOHANG` at all: 5** (4 at HEAD plus the uncommitted arm_msrmode). **OF THOSE FIVE, HOW MANY SAMPLE waitpid ONCE?**  `pcc2_width_probe.py` polls 30x0.1s and waitpid only fills `how`; `pcc2_c040_probe.py` the same; `xscale_inten_probe.py` polls 2s in `close()` and sets `self.dead` on EOF during `send()`; `arm_msrmode_probe.py` polls 12s. `luna_absentcpu_probe.py` **does sample once -- and it is NOT the alive oracle**, being called from `died()` only after `step_at` has already failed on EOF.  **ONCE-ONLY IN THE LIVE TREE: 1.  WAITPID-ONCE AS THE SURVIVE ORACLE: 0.** *** AND THE SEAT NAMED THE CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN THE KEYWORD, which is what makes this reusable: the bug is NOT 'has WNOHANG'.  It is the three-part combination -- `rd()` returns on an empty `os.read` so the spin is skipped exactly on death; that return is IGNORED; and `alive` is then taken from a single `waitpid(WNOHANG)`.  Any one of the three alone is harmless. ***  **DISPOSITION: NO TREE-WIDE EDIT.**  The seat's own words -- *'a tree-wide rewrite would manufacture findings'* -- and this project's addition licence agree: 33 EOF-as-alive probes consume `rd()`'s return and are correct as written.  The boundary is recorded so a future round does not rediscover the class and sweep it.",
50635:     "note": "*** CENSUSED 2026-09-17 AND THE CLASS IS CLOSED WITH ITS DENOMINATOR: **0 shipped live probes still mis-score this way.**  The defect was born today and died today. ***  The founding case is `regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py`, which had the exact shape, was MEASURED reporting `alive` for a process that had SIGABRT'd, and was rewritten to poll the same hour.  `arm_msrmode_probe.py` was built with the polling form from the start. **METHOD, keyed on MECHANISM rather than on names** -- and it explicitly refused to count `artifacts/**` frozen copies, which would have inflated the class about FIFTEENFOLD by re-counting the same five files: live population is `regress/*.py` = **99 files**, minus 10 harness/selftest/census scripts and one source-only probe = **88 launchers**. **THE DEATH-AS-ORACLE FAMILIES, with counts:** EOF-as-alive (`alive = rd(...)`) **33**; sessions borrowed from those 33 **11** (pcc2_default execs pcc2_width's session; ten SH4 probes import sh4_pcic_probe); prompt/dump still-answering **3**; `subprocess.run` wait-status **6**; **`WNOHANG` at all: 5** (4 at HEAD plus the uncommitted arm_msrmode). **OF THOSE FIVE, HOW MANY SAMPLE waitpid ONCE?**  `pcc2_width_probe.py` polls 30x0.1s and waitpid only fills `how`; `pcc2_c040_probe.py` the same; `xscale_inten_probe.py` polls 2s in `close()` and sets `self.dead` on EOF during `send()`; `arm_msrmode_probe.py` polls 12s. `luna_absentcpu_probe.py` **does sample once -- and it is NOT the alive oracle**, being called from `died()` only after `step_at` has already failed on EOF.  **ONCE-ONLY IN THE LIVE TREE: 1.  WAITPID-ONCE AS THE SURVIVE ORACLE: 0.** *** AND THE SEAT NAMED THE CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN THE KEYWORD, which is what makes this reusable: the bug is NOT 'has WNOHANG'.  It is the three-part combination -- `rd()` returns on an empty `os.read` so the spin is skipped exactly on death; that return is IGNORED; and `alive` is then taken from a single `waitpid(WNOHANG)`.  Any one of the three alone is harmless. ***  **DISPOSITION: NO TREE-WIDE EDIT.**  The seat's own words -- *'a tree-wide rewrite would manufacture findings'* -- and this project's addition licence agree: 33 EOF-as-alive probes consume `rd()`'s return and are correct as written.  The boundary is recorded so a future round does not rediscover the class and sweep it.",
51405:     "ev": "regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/opus_killtable_20260917/isrsem.log",
51418:   "state_note": "FILED 2026-09-17 by the #531 pass-2 opus5 seat as the nearest SIBLING of ip30abortkill.  Two structurally identical `fatal(\"TODO: ip22 legacy interrupt rewrite!\"); abort();' pairs in dev_sgi_ip22.c, in the WRITE arms of the local0 and local1 interrupt masks.  *** THE CENSUS LESSON RECURS: these carry no `exit(', so the same three exit( sweeps that walked past #531's four sites walk past these too.  A census keyed on `exit(' cannot see a host death spelled abort(). ***  Ranked HIGH on the same warrant as #531: guest-reachable host death on an advertised machine. The disposition is likely the same as #531's -- heart.h has no ip22 equivalent, so the option-set work starts from the file's own sibling handlers.  LINE NUMBERS VERIFIED 2026-09-17 by opening the file: :314 and :338 exactly, 2 abort() and 0 exit( in dev_sgi_ip22.c.  Grade upgraded BELIEVED -> CONFIRMED.  *** SEVERITY CORRECTED HIGH -> LOW THE SAME DAY IT WAS FILED, AND THE CORRECTION IS MINE TO OWN: I RANKED IT AS A SIBLING OF #531 WITHOUT CHECKING THE ONE FACT THAT MADE #531 LIVE. ***  #531's warrant is that `-E sgi -e ip30' is an ADVERTISED machine AND the device is actually installed -- its rung-3 probe reached the code and killed the host, empirically.  dev_sgi_ip22 is DIFFERENT and the difference is decisive:  (a) `dev_sgi_ip22_init' has exactly TWO call sites in the whole tree, machine_sgi.c:270 and :278, and BOTH ARE COMMENTED OUT;  (b) the file defines DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_ip22) but NO DEVINIT(sgi_ip22), so the autodev / device_add route cannot register it either;  (c) it still COMPILES IN (Makefile.skel lists dev_sgi_ip22.o), which is why an abort()-census finds it and a reachability question does not get asked.  *** THE DEVICE IS NEVER IN ANY MACHINE'S MEMORY MAP, SO NO GUEST CAN REACH EITHER abort(). ***  CONSEQUENCE FOR THE WITNESS LADDER, and it is why this cannot simply be 'done later': NO WITNESS EXISTS OR CAN EXIST AT RUNGS 2-4 while the device is uninstalled, and installing it to reach the site is exactly what the ladder names as LAUNDERING -- 'a machine or device_add introduced IN ORDER TO reach the site is laundering, not witnessing'.  So this is DOCUMENTED-ONLY unless and until something installs the device for its own reasons.  IT REMAINS WORTH KEEPING rather than dropping: the sites are dead code carrying a host kill, and the day anyone re-enables those two commented lines they become live immediately, with no review in between.  *** THE CENSUS LESSON STANDS UNCHANGED AND IS THE REAL VALUE HERE: 2 abort() and 0 exit( in this file, so the same three exit( sweeps that walked past #531's four sites walk past these two. ***  A census keyed on `exit(' cannot see a host death spelled abort() -- whether or not the code is reachable.",
51448:   "state_note": "*** THE FOURTH RECORDED INSTANCE OF THE UNREAD-REVIEW CLASS, AND THE MOST PRECISE: THE MISSING ROW WAS PRESCRIBED BY NAME, IN ONE LINE, IN A DURABLE ARTIFACT, BEFORE THE FIX SHIPPED. ***  regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/FIXDIFF_grok_20260917.txt:239 reads: '5. `isr 20 rd' / `isr 28 rd' -- load does not clobber ISR; load's VALUE is not the seeded ISR (don't-mirror)'.  BOTH rows, explicitly.  The round shipped `isr 20 rd val' and not its sibling, and it then cost a full extra kill table and a nine-seat adjudication pass to rediscover -- with agy REQUIRING it and grok having to point at its own earlier answer.  The opus5 seat independently reported the same pattern: grok's design pass prescribed six closing rows and items 1, 2, 4 and 5 did not ship.  *** THE STRUCTURAL GAP, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING: THE CARRIER'S EXISTING RULE CANNOT CATCH THIS. ***  After #490 the rule is 'a row list rewritten from a panel's findings is DIFFED against the pre-table block's own prescribed rows, not merely extended with the new ones.'  That binds the PRETABLE.  Here the prescription NEVER ENTERED A PRETABLE -- it lived in a SEAT'S FIX-DESIGN ANSWER, and nothing diffs a row list against that.  So the #490 rule was obeyed and the row was still lost: the diff ran against the wrong source document.  AND THE PRETABLE MADE IT WORSE RATHER THAN NEUTRAL: PRETABLE.out listed BOTH read arms as 'decline, no value to pin', so the one artifact #490 DOES mandate diffing against positively asserted that neither row was owed.  *A pre-table block that mis-classifies a cell does not merely fail to catch the omission; it CERTIFIES it.*  grok's correction is one sentence: A DECLINE HAS A VALUE, AND IT IS 0.  PROPOSED REMEDY, FILED NOT BUILT (a harness change owing two negative controls): a round whose fix design was reviewed by a seat DIFFS ITS FINAL ROW LIST AGAINST THAT SEAT'S PRESCRIBED ROWS, as #490 mandates for the PRETABLE -- and the PRETABLE should CARRY those prescriptions forward so the two documents cannot disagree silently.  Cheapest mechanical form is existence-only: if a FIXDIFF_<seat>_*.txt sits beside the killtable dir, each of its numbered prescriptions must map to a shipped row or an explicit no-row sentence.  *** THE LAST FIVE UNREAD ANSWERS READ 2026-09-18 (panel_20260827_134019).  23 OF 23 NOW READ -- the section-G backlog is CLEARED. ***  This was a pass-1 DESIGN panel on a now-CLOSED row, so it was read for the question `seatprescriptiondiff' exists to ask: DID THE PRESCRIPTIONS SURVIVE INTO THE SHIPPED WORK?  *** AND THE ANSWER IS YES -- A NEGATIVE RESULT THAT BOUNDS THE ROW I FILED THIS MORNING. ***  agy prescribed three items.  (1) the predicate fix -- SHIPPED, dev_wdc.c now triggers on WDCTL_RST (0x04) and not WDCTL_4BIT (0x08), with the rising-edge `prev_ctl' machinery and a recorded brace hazard beside it.  (2) the MACHINE_LANDISK alt-status mapping -- NOT in dev_wdc.c, and NOT a silent drop: it was SPLIT INTO ITS OWN ROW `landiskaux', which is open, and OUTSTANDING_BUGS carries the coupling in full.  (3) acceptance rows -- folded, per the kimi/deepseek rulings in the same panel.  *** SO `seatprescriptiondiff' HAS A POPULATION OF ONE (the #531 case), NOT A PATTERN.  A class filed from a single instance is a hypothesis, and this is the first test of it -- it did not generalise.  Recorded as such rather than left looking systemic. ***  AND THE COUPLING WAS HANDLED IN THE SAFE ORDER, which is worth keeping because the unsafe one was live: mapping the landisk register WHILE the predicate still triggered on 0x08 would have latched COMMAND_RESET on SIX routine Device Control writes per probe (a seat measured twelve writes, six of them 0x08, currently all landing on unmapped memory).  The round fixed the PREDICATE first, so `wdcaltctrlbit' is CLOSED as overtaken and `landiskaux' is now OPEN AND UNBLOCKED.  *** THAT MAKES `landiskaux' A ONE-LINE FIX THAT IS NOW SAFE TO TAKE -- a strong critical-and-easily-resolvable candidate for the next round. ***  The other seats' content was design judgement, no live defects: glm listed SEVEN uninlined premises and ranked them by load-bearingness (the premise-audit discipline working as intended); minimax named an option-set hole (C4/B5, 'the brief's C-options jump'); deepseek ruled that a channel reset must clear in-flight transfer, FIFO, phase and interrupt state but NOT per-device-life diagnostics like `warned_*' -- and dev_wdc.c carries 43 `warned_' references, so that distinction is load-bearing there.",
51456:     "ev": "regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/FIXDIFF_grok_20260917.txt:239",

